[[:db/retract 17592186198639 :question/answer-fields 17592186194465] {:db/id 17592186198410 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-66286cd3-980b-5dcd-96d4-d9a56bcaa6b2" "question-1750e7bf-7e92-5681-92a1-454eb28ef5bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198408 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4c3e83a3-697e-51c3-b71e-01fe636e3df8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198409 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-70f7151e-4f69-5e76-9c39-e06e4443c9a7" "question-86915a7f-cf68-50dc-aafb-5f62c6d2e7e3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-66286cd3-980b-5dcd-96d4-d9a56bcaa6b2" :question/id #uuid "66286cd3-980b-5dcd-96d4-d9a56bcaa6b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163014" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $1\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{3}-3,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=4{x}^{3}-3,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4{x}^{3}-3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{x}^{4}-3x]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(16-6)-(1-3) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $12\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a83eb5c9-f2db-5800-a452-9042bb3f229a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a83eb5c9-f2db-5800-a452-9042bb3f229a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a83eb5c9-f2db-5800-a452-9042bb3f229a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb621112-9f81-5797-a79f-6c7d609cfae5" "answer-f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" "answer-bfd2b78a-a10b-5a1b-befb-dfe0ee645ba4" "answer-6834cafa-e224-515f-8cd2-a32f4c4a3f9a" "answer-b19d0976-e6d7-5e98-9b30-7b81b0dfbad4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb621112-9f81-5797-a79f-6c7d609cfae5" :answer/id #uuid "bb621112-9f81-5797-a79f-6c7d609cfae5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" :answer/id #uuid "f26fedd6-1d79-5b53-a483-c5459c6e306f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfd2b78a-a10b-5a1b-befb-dfe0ee645ba4" :answer/id #uuid "bfd2b78a-a10b-5a1b-befb-dfe0ee645ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6834cafa-e224-515f-8cd2-a32f4c4a3f9a" :answer/id #uuid "6834cafa-e224-515f-8cd2-a32f4c4a3f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b19d0976-e6d7-5e98-9b30-7b81b0dfbad4" :answer/id #uuid "b19d0976-e6d7-5e98-9b30-7b81b0dfbad4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1750e7bf-7e92-5681-92a1-454eb28ef5bc" :question/id #uuid "1750e7bf-7e92-5681-92a1-454eb28ef5bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-163010" :question/problem "The mass density function $\\lambda ,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ of a thin rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2$ is given by $\\lambda (x)=x+2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?" :question/worked-solution "Given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b,$ if $\\lambda (x)$ denotes the mass density function of the rod, then the total mass of the rod is given by  \n\n$$\nm={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=x+2,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe calculate the mass of the rod as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x+2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{2}+2\\cdot 2)-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the rod is $6\\,\\text{kg}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a609109-bbc5-5a2b-88f8-b2bbf1867c8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a609109-bbc5-5a2b-88f8-b2bbf1867c8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a609109-bbc5-5a2b-88f8-b2bbf1867c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1951745b-12ed-540f-b8d2-2e76d8598187" "answer-b3ef9a26-6009-519a-ae29-9fbcd3b3c4cf" "answer-5b862d6f-8f37-5068-9257-f93374bc563f" "answer-c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" "answer-2b2eba11-f54c-5b8d-8056-31c66238b541"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1951745b-12ed-540f-b8d2-2e76d8598187" :answer/id #uuid "1951745b-12ed-540f-b8d2-2e76d8598187" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3ef9a26-6009-519a-ae29-9fbcd3b3c4cf" :answer/id #uuid "b3ef9a26-6009-519a-ae29-9fbcd3b3c4cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b862d6f-8f37-5068-9257-f93374bc563f" :answer/id #uuid "5b862d6f-8f37-5068-9257-f93374bc563f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" :answer/id #uuid "c1d321ac-e140-5cfc-af54-9379710575c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2b2eba11-f54c-5b8d-8056-31c66238b541" :answer/id #uuid "2b2eba11-f54c-5b8d-8056-31c66238b541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198639 :question/problem "![](images/d6/d64311921135cf8dea0ec70bb0a83909fb1dba52664f4d6080de596be1693d5e.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2\\,\\text{kg/m}.$ Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+2,\\,a=1,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+{2}^{2})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}+{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4} \\\\  & =6.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd13b3c7-3da9-5394-8668-03f8c929a5e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd13b3c7-3da9-5394-8668-03f8c929a5e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd13b3c7-3da9-5394-8668-03f8c929a5e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e14c0f00-36c9-598c-96a2-ba74927d341f" "answer-1d449c1e-1f46-5f61-9ad7-f822f5f2a1f0" "answer-d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" "answer-9a21ab4f-abbb-53fc-b207-1a91a7fd1b51" "answer-ffcb4221-1176-5d9c-9580-81276d2bd08f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e14c0f00-36c9-598c-96a2-ba74927d341f" :answer/id #uuid "e14c0f00-36c9-598c-96a2-ba74927d341f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d449c1e-1f46-5f61-9ad7-f822f5f2a1f0" :answer/id #uuid "1d449c1e-1f46-5f61-9ad7-f822f5f2a1f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" :answer/id #uuid "d44b3ce5-4e08-5925-ab10-8a405b4e7b97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.75\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a21ab4f-abbb-53fc-b207-1a91a7fd1b51" :answer/id #uuid "9a21ab4f-abbb-53fc-b207-1a91a7fd1b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ffcb4221-1176-5d9c-9580-81276d2bd08f" :answer/id #uuid "ffcb4221-1176-5d9c-9580-81276d2bd08f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4c3e83a3-697e-51c3-b71e-01fe636e3df8" :question/id #uuid "4c3e83a3-697e-51c3-b71e-01fe636e3df8" :question/math-academy-id "q-163040" :question/problem "A thin rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+1,$ measured in $\\text{kg/m},$ is placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 2,$ where $x$ is measured in meters. Find the moment of the rod about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda (x)$ for $a\\le x\\le b$ is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)={x}^{2}+1,\\,a=0,\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the moment of the rod about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the required moment is $6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b97a16d2-6774-5dbd-8c93-1bf19e34efa2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b97a16d2-6774-5dbd-8c93-1bf19e34efa2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b97a16d2-6774-5dbd-8c93-1bf19e34efa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ebcc29e-8dc5-5b22-b315-99b116bd7c52" "answer-bc9a5b2c-67cb-5952-b3aa-930af2c44107" "answer-5f93a53e-5bf0-5586-a8d2-b6408a97c494" "answer-ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" "answer-794447c6-52f5-5724-9803-b4e438995276"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ebcc29e-8dc5-5b22-b315-99b116bd7c52" :answer/id #uuid "4ebcc29e-8dc5-5b22-b315-99b116bd7c52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc9a5b2c-67cb-5952-b3aa-930af2c44107" :answer/id #uuid "bc9a5b2c-67cb-5952-b3aa-930af2c44107" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f93a53e-5bf0-5586-a8d2-b6408a97c494" :answer/id #uuid "5f93a53e-5bf0-5586-a8d2-b6408a97c494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" :answer/id #uuid "ef2a88f5-6bb1-5f1a-8872-83524ff4e528" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-794447c6-52f5-5724-9803-b4e438995276" :answer/id #uuid "794447c6-52f5-5724-9803-b4e438995276" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70f7151e-4f69-5e76-9c39-e06e4443c9a7" :question/id #uuid "70f7151e-4f69-5e76-9c39-e06e4443c9a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-163029" :question/problem "Consider a thin rod along the $x$-axis over the interval $0\\le x\\le 1$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}+1.$ Find the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass of the rod." :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=6{x}^{2}+1,\\,a=0,\\,b=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}+1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}+x]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2+1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot (6{x}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-66d54e84-a316-51a7-bfbb-7e33fe6a2ed2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-66d54e84-a316-51a7-bfbb-7e33fe6a2ed2" :answer-field/id #uuid "66d54e84-a316-51a7-bfbb-7e33fe6a2ed2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" "answer-60ed81d6-0a1b-546f-9241-8d1dbe590600" "answer-d7875743-53eb-5b08-8c40-19648e5ae5e6" "answer-ac9b88b6-65b8-5f2b-b100-faa9a5a6d1a6" "answer-4a2af5bd-c1ed-59d9-a566-4a0c218db269"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" :answer/id #uuid "da5a0437-0721-5097-9076-84f467dcd2f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60ed81d6-0a1b-546f-9241-8d1dbe590600" :answer/id #uuid "60ed81d6-0a1b-546f-9241-8d1dbe590600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7875743-53eb-5b08-8c40-19648e5ae5e6" :answer/id #uuid "d7875743-53eb-5b08-8c40-19648e5ae5e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac9b88b6-65b8-5f2b-b100-faa9a5a6d1a6" :answer/id #uuid "ac9b88b6-65b8-5f2b-b100-faa9a5a6d1a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a2af5bd-c1ed-59d9-a566-4a0c218db269" :answer/id #uuid "4a2af5bd-c1ed-59d9-a566-4a0c218db269" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-86915a7f-cf68-50dc-aafb-5f62c6d2e7e3" :question/id #uuid "86915a7f-cf68-50dc-aafb-5f62c6d2e7e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-163020" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad5a7d1121f6ae5a471f78477a8857b75c6a5a2008e769b1b9115c2ac880d5b6.png)\n\nThe thin rod above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.$ Given that the mass of the rod is $\\frac{9}{2}$ units, what is the $x$-coordinate of its center of mass?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a rod placed along the $x$-axis over the interval $a\\le x\\le b$ whose mass density function is $\\lambda (x)$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the mass of the rod,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\,x\\lambda (x)\\,\\text{d}x$ is the moment of the rod about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}},\\,a=1,\\,b=8.\n$$\n\nSo,  the moment of the rod about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{8}{x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}]}_{1}^{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(32-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{93}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{(\\frac{93}{5})}{(\\frac{9}{2})}=\\frac{62}{15}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1acb675f-5ff9-554d-a90a-36c18f959baf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1acb675f-5ff9-554d-a90a-36c18f959baf" :answer-field/id #uuid "1acb675f-5ff9-554d-a90a-36c18f959baf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52814006-a528-5e8d-b83f-56a2cb50f1ce" "answer-b252df5d-3385-541f-8009-fb9c2955cb06" "answer-a7a0bf2c-4e79-5ebe-80ea-3bd71ad1bd01" "answer-13212333-e1f8-56ff-a8c7-3198d8cdf406" "answer-85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52814006-a528-5e8d-b83f-56a2cb50f1ce" :answer/id #uuid "52814006-a528-5e8d-b83f-56a2cb50f1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b252df5d-3385-541f-8009-fb9c2955cb06" :answer/id #uuid "b252df5d-3385-541f-8009-fb9c2955cb06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{29}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7a0bf2c-4e79-5ebe-80ea-3bd71ad1bd01" :answer/id #uuid "a7a0bf2c-4e79-5ebe-80ea-3bd71ad1bd01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13212333-e1f8-56ff-a8c7-3198d8cdf406" :answer/id #uuid "13212333-e1f8-56ff-a8c7-3198d8cdf406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{49}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603" :answer/id #uuid "85946e32-9875-5ae9-b212-a1791298f603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{62}{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199486 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll learn how to determine the center of mass of a thin rod whose mass is unevenly distributed. \n\nWe describe the mass distribution along a thin rod using a so-called **mass density function** $\\lambda (x).$ This function tells us the *mass per unit length* at any point $x$ on the rod. The units of $\\lambda$ are usually $\\textrm{kg}/\\textrm{m}.$\n\nConsider a thin rod between the points $x=1$ and $x=3$ along the $x$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c9ee70d28476ebda61ccce5c6342a7f1a48a3e0f4dc26ee1af147d6f3d34a218.png)\n\n \n\nSuppose the mass density function of the rod is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x) = 3x^2 \\, \\textrm{kg/m},\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is measured in meters. What is the total mass of the rod?\n\nTo answer this, consider a point $x \\in (1,3)$ on the rod and cut out a small piece of length $\\Delta{x},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/9b/9b62c29b499159fe23e9ece7023ed179f4565600a88677fe51ab002a4a0d6faf.png)\n\n \n\nIf $\\Delta{x}$ is very small, we can assume that our density function is approximately constant over the selected piece. As a result, the mass of this piece is\n\n$$\n\\Delta{m} \\approx 3x^2 \\Delta{x}.\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\Delta{m}$ are \n$\\dfrac{\\textrm{kg}}{\\textrm{m}} \\cdot \\textrm{m} = \\textrm{kg},$\nas we'd expect.\n\nTo find the total mass of the rod, we add together the masses of all such pieces and take the limit as $\\Delta x \\to 0.$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\nm =  \\int_{1}^{3} 3x^2 \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nCarrying out the integration, we find that the total mass of the rod is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{3}-{1}^{3} \\\\  & =26\\,\\text{kg}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, given a thin rod oriented along the $x$-axis over the interval $a \\leq x \\leq b,$ if $\\lambda(x)$ denotes the rod's mass density function, then the total mass of the rod is given by\n\n$$\nm = \\int_a^b \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199490 :tutorial/content "In a previous lesson, we saw how to calculate the total moment about the origin of a collection of masses distributed along the $x$-axis. We'll now extend our understanding to include moments of thin rods.\n\nConsider a thin rod between the points $x=1$ and $x=3$ along the $x$-axis with mass density function $\\lambda(x) = 3x^2 \\, \\textrm{kg/m},$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c9/c9ee70d28476ebda61ccce5c6342a7f1a48a3e0f4dc26ee1af147d6f3d34a218.png)\n\nHow can we find the total moment of the rod about the origin?\n\nTo answer this, we once again consider a small piece of rod located in the interval $(x, x+\\Delta x),$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/fd/fd2dc58c503333a365b140de3ef1b559477788953dab14549478ca031df98125.png)\n\n \n\nIf $\\Delta{x}$ is very small, we can approximate this piece as a point mass. \n\nThe moment of this piece about the origin, denoted $\\Delta{M_O},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ{M}_{O} & ≈x\\cdot Δm \\\\  & ≈x\\cdot \\lambda (x)Δx \\\\  & =x\\cdot 3{x}^{2}Δx \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}Δx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, to find the moment of the entire rod about the origin, we sum the moments of all such pieces and take the limit as $\\Delta x.$ By doing so, we get \n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_{1}^{3} 3x^3 \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this integral, we find that the total moment about $O$ of the rod is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3)^{4}}{4}-\\frac{3(1)^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =60\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn general, the moment about the origin of a rod with mass density function $\\lambda(x)$ for $a \\leq x \\leq b$ is given by\n\n$$\nM_O = \\int_a^b x\\, \\lambda(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198496 :activity/expected-seconds 600.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
